{"citation": "Analyst calculation from the § 77.19 50:1 slope: maximum object height = distance from surface origin ÷ 50; a 50-ft object reaches the surface at ~2,500 ft, a 70-ft object at ~3,500 ft. Assumes flat terrain at runway-end elevation pending the operator's surveyed site plan.", "claim": "A 50-foot object reaches the 50:1 approach surface only about 2,500 feet beyond the runway end.", "claim_id": "C-06", "evidence_ids": ["quantitative-analyst::E-0042"], "footnote_id": "4", "primary_source_checked": true, "retained": true, "verification_note": "Arithmetic from the verified 50:1 slope: 50 × 50 = 2,500 ft. Correctly labeled as analyst calculation pending site survey.", "verification_status": "verified"}
