{"citation": "Analyst calculation from standard 3-degree glidepath geometry (50 ft threshold crossing height): overflight height ≈ 102 ft AGL at 1,000 ft from threshold, ~207 ft at 3,000 ft.", "claim": "Aircraft overflying the parcel is roughly 100 feet above the ground at 1,000 feet from the threshold, about 200 feet at 3,000 feet.", "claim_id": "C-09", "evidence_ids": ["quantitative-analyst::E-0046"], "footnote_id": "6", "primary_source_checked": false, "retained": true, "verification_note": "Standard 3° ILS glidepath geometry: height = 50 + (distance_ft × tan 3°). At 1,000 ft: 102 ft; at 3,000 ft: 207 ft. Rounded correctly in draft ('roughly 100,' 'about 200').", "verification_status": "verified"}
{"citation": "FAA AC 150/5200-33C, Hazardous Wildlife Attractants on or Near Airports, recommends 10,000 ft separation between a hazardous wildlife attractant and the aircraft operations area for airports serving turbine-powered aircraft. The ~95% figure is an analyst estimate based on the physical proximity of a runway-end pond to the threshold; actual shortfall depends on the surveyed site plan.", "claim": "FAA guidance asks for 10,000 feet of separation between a wildlife attractant and turbine operations.", "claim_id": "C-10", "draft_sha256": "2e96b9545a4c131c5a6c8d406ebf0fe2e0fc1df4a2a85460464a52d2e20d7542", "evidence_ids": ["quantitative-analyst::E-0044", "operations-analyst::E-0034"], "footnote_id": "7", "primary_source_checked": true, "retained": true, "verification_note": "AC 150/5200-33B/C 10,000 ft turbine-aircraft separation distance confirmed in evidence ledger quote. Footnote updated to cite current revision 33C.", "verification_status": "verified"}
{"citation": "FAA AC 150/5200-33C, Hazardous Wildlife Attractants on or Near Airports, recommends 10,000 ft separation between a hazardous wildlife attractant and the aircraft operations area for airports serving turbine-powered aircraft. The ~95% figure is an analyst estimate based on the physical proximity of a runway-end pond to the threshold; actual shortfall depends on the surveyed site plan.", "claim": "A pond at the runway end sits roughly 95 percent inside the 10,000-foot wildlife separation standard.", "claim_id": "C-11", "evidence_ids": ["quantitative-analyst::E-0045"], "footnote_id": "7", "primary_source_checked": false, "retained": true, "verification_note": "95% figure is an analyst calculation assuming ~500 ft actual distance (10,000 - 500)/10,000 = 95%. E-0045 caveat notes actual separation is a placeholder pending the surveyed site plan. Footnote in final draft discloses this dependency. Even at a generous 2,000 ft actual, the pond is 80% inside the standard (per E-0045 caveat).", "verification_status": "qualified"}
